{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.5076217197052523, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No sign of getting around the measurement. Atom-pair fingerprints are computed from the test SMILES only as unsupervised features. No test labels, file access or pasted values are used. Stacking uses scaffold-grouped out-of-fold predictions, so there is no leakage.", "No bug that would make the result meaningless. A sum of two Tanimoto kernels is still a valid kernel, and the same combination is used for fitting and prediction.", "The edit changes several things at once: it adds an atom-pair kernel, halves the LightGBM rounds while doubling the learning rate, halves the random forest trees and drops the lambda/wr grid search to one fixed setting. That makes it impossible to tell which change caused the loss to get worse. Also, the summed Tanimoto kernel roughly doubles the kernel scale, so the fixed lam=0.5 is effectively weaker regularization than before.", "Recomputed z = (0.4895 - 0.5076) / (0.0042*sqrt(2)) \u2248 -3.05, which matches the harness value of -3.055. The candidate is worse by about 0.018, and the reject decision is consistent."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Cut runtime by shrinking the KRR hyperparameter grid, using fewer boosting rounds at a higher learning rate, and using fewer RF trees.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "spruce", "idea_id": "b019", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.4894866999475836, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.4894866999475836, "n": 1}, "job_id": "B1_lipo_HH_1_cs0-crash_fix-12_1795052657575", "kind": "crash_fix", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.0261705, "cost_usd_plan": 0.0261705, "latency_s": 10.34875597403152, "requested_model": "sonnet", "role": "repairer", "served_model": "sonnet", "tokens_in": 4880, "tokens_out": 1190}, {"cost_usd_nominal": 0.0204185, "cost_usd_plan": 0.0204185, "latency_s": 3.7618534690118395, "req